{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/911496-a-promethean-gameline-for-owod","id":911496,"title":"A Promethean gameline for OWoD?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-09T23:45:49-07:00","id":911496,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> A Promethean gameline for OWoD?","content":"So, somebody brought up the idea of creating versions of some of the new lines from Chronicles as part of World, and I think Promethean could a great choice for this.<br /> &quot;A Storytelling Game of Stolen Lives&quot;, but re-imagined to ACTUALLY <u>BE</u> ABOUT <i>STOLEN LIVES</i>!<br /> \u200bAside from the OVERWHELMING supernatural downsides of the Promethean condition, a major issue I've heard from people is that several of the listed inspirations are love stories, stories about someone who will stop at NOTHING to see a loved one restored to them. Instead, P:tC gives them a blank slate; some...THING, wearing the face of the person the were trying to revive. So, what if there was a game about trying to return to life? I know Wraith kind of covers that, but I still think there could be some merit to a game in which your character is returned to a semblance of life, and has to choose between finishing the process and returning to their former life, or building a new one. Even if part of the metaphysics of the game is that the revived is NOT the same being as the one whose body they were made from, starting off with some memories, and hopefully someone who <i>cares</i>, who wants desperately to have that person back, might make existence more tolerable; less depressing. It still raises plenty of existential and philosophical questions, and I think it could work pretty well for small, intimate gaming groups. Thoughts?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":6138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","user":"Mangle77","date":". 08-21-2016, 10:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T01:21:56-07:00","id":911523,"title":"","content":"Some time ago a friend and I dreamed up Promethean: The Genesis as a sort of cWoD Prommie. Strongly inspired by Alan Moore's run on Swamp Thing. The general pitch was thus:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The world of men is coming to a close, our last hurrah a tar choked coughing fit. But who is to inherit the earth in man's absence? Enter Prometheans, each their own Adam or Eve, first of their kind. Unencumbered with original sin they arise now to bear witness to the end, to learn from the errors of God's mistake and perhaps give rise to a better race. But not all Prometheans are content to sit out and observe humanity's decline, some seek to aid man, others to depose us faster, and yet more fall into the same traps of sin that damned the human race. Which will you be? </div> </div> </div>Obviously this was aimed at cWoDs more...cut and dry universe and general religious overtones. It was also a thought experiment on inversion, making cWoD Prommie something different from CofD while keeping some of the same feel. The Created remain works of man and nature, but the New Dawn is shifted from a personal goal to a universal paradigm shift (to borrow the phrase from Ascension). Disquiet occurs because humans, encumbered by original sin, cannot tolerate the spirital purity of Prometheans and seek to drag them down. Wasteland is reskinned as the Promethean unconsciously creating a personal eden, paradise for themselves, but not necessarily for man.<br /> <br /> Looking back now we sunk quite a lot of thought into it, but it never really advanced beyond musing.<br /> <br /> Dunno if any of that is useful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T02:39:13-07:00","id":911543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PenDragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/911496-a-promethean-gameline-for-owod?p=911523#post911523\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some time ago a friend and I dreamed up Promethean: The Genesis as a sort of cWoD Prommie. Strongly inspired by Alan Moore's run on Swamp Thing. The general pitch was thus:<br /> <br /> Obviously this was aimed at cWoDs more...cut and dry universe and general religious overtones. It was also a thought experiment on inversion, making cWoD Prommie something different from CofD while keeping some of the same feel. The Created remain works of man and nature, but the New Dawn is shifted from a personal goal to a universal paradigm shift (to borrow the phrase from Ascension). Disquiet occurs because humans, encumbered by original sin, cannot tolerate the spirital purity of Prometheans and seek to drag them down. Wasteland is reskinned as the Promethean unconsciously creating a personal eden, paradise for themselves, but not necessarily for man.<br /> <br /> Looking back now we sunk quite a lot of thought into it, but it never really advanced beyond musing.<br /> <br /> Dunno if any of that is useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T10:16:05-07:00","id":911740,"title":"","content":"It's worth mentioning that there's a Mage book (it might be Storyteller's Handbook Rev.) that discusses a period of time in Mage history roughly around the 1800's when it was <i>all the rage</i> to make Frankenstein-type monsters (which based on my limited understanding of CoD, is essentially what <i>Prometheans</i> are). In any case, as I recall the text referred to this time period as like a rueful thing--like people were making these creatures left and right and it was constant bother or annoyance.<br /> <br /> May be worth looking into!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T06:20:54-07:00","id":914050,"title":"","content":"How can it be &quot;left and right&quot; if it takes AT LEAST Master level Life to create one?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T09:05:27-07:00","id":914124,"title":"","content":"Well, not really. Creating a perfect human body its Life 5. Stitching together some corpses and giving them a horrible semblance of life could be much easier.<br /> <br /> That explains the rage...<br /> <br /> However, for a, let's say, &quot;nobler&quot; beast you would like to have at least Mind 5 and Spirits 5-to create a true soul and inteligence to the being. Life 5 if you want it to have a neat perfect body (but what's the <i>fun</i> of that).<br /> <br /> EDIT: Life 5, Mind 5, Spirit 5 it's a legendary Rote that creates a true human being.<br /> It could be interesting, for a &quot;Frankenstein era&quot;, to study possible workarounds that mages of the age could have done to reduce the required Sphere levels to a more reasonable amount...and the consecuences of such &quot;savings&quot;<br /> For instance, Life 3 (maybe with Matter 2) could be enough to restore functionality to bodyparts of several bodies. Spirit 5 creates a true human soul, but you could use Spirit 4 to seal a spirit inside the carcass, to move it and think (no need of Mind 5 at all). Which could have interesting results. Of course such a creature can't be called human. <i>But that's the whole point, isn't it?</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 06-14-2016, 12:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T10:10:39-07:00","id":914167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/911496-a-promethean-gameline-for-owod?p=914124#post914124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, not really. Creating a perfect human body its Life 5. Stitching together some corpses and giving them a horrible semblance of life could be much easier.<br /> <br /> That explains the rage...<br /> <br /> However, for a, let's say, &quot;nobler&quot; beast you would like to have at least Mind 5 and Spirits 5-to create a true soul and inteligence to the being. Life 5 if you want it to have a neat perfect body (but what's the <i>fun</i> of that).<br /> <br /> EDIT: Life 5, Mind 5, Spirit 5 it's a legendary Rote that creates a true human being.<br /> It could be interesting, for a &quot;Frankenstein era&quot;, to study possible workarounds that mages of the age could have done to reduce the required Sphere levels to a more reasonable amount...and the consecuences of such &quot;savings&quot;<br /> For instance, Life 3 (maybe with Matter 2) could be enough to restore functionality to bodyparts of several bodies. Spirit 5 creates a true human soul, but you could use Spirit 4 to seal a spirit inside the carcass, to move it and think (no need of Mind 5 at all). Which could have interesting results. Of course such a creature can't be called human. <i>But that's the whole point, isn't it?</i></div> </div> </div> </div>How about not even trying to make a Fetish Frankenstein and just Awakening the stitched together mess? If you can Awaken a house or a car, or even a heap of trash, you should be able to Awaken the spirit of a carefully articulated complete set of human-parts. I guess, if they all came from different people, maybe Prime 2 to create a more &quot;unified Pattern&quot; for the whole thing instead of several joined together higglety-pigglety.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T10:28:44-07:00","id":914189,"title":"","content":"True, and then you will have a spirit/entity that has reasons to believe itself human or at least to identify with humanity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T14:48:26-07:00","id":914392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/911496-a-promethean-gameline-for-owod?p=911740#post911740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's worth mentioning that there's a Mage book (it might be Storyteller's Handbook Rev.) that discusses a period of time in Mage history roughly around the 1800's when it was <i>all the rage</i> to make Frankenstein-type monsters (which based on my limited understanding of CoD, is essentially what <i>Prometheans</i> are). In any case, as I recall the text referred to this time period as like a rueful thing--like people were making these creatures left and right and it was constant bother or annoyance.<br /> <br /> May be worth looking into!</div> </div> </div> </div>It was the wonderful time when the propagators of mystic, weird science and proper science Paradigms all thought their way of doing things had an equal right to exist in the world - or perhaps indeed, the right to rule over it! One of ways to prove it was indeed the creation of new life, and letting those beings out into the world. :-)<br /> <br /> By XX century, the people behind the weird science paradigm got defeated and side-lined. No more prometheans running around. And belief in mysticism and esotericism started losing ground to scientific though and methods.<br /> ( Hopefully I haven't simplified things too much in this post :&gt;. )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 06-14-2016, 05:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T07:34:15-07:00","id":916184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/911496-a-promethean-gameline-for-owod?p=911740#post911740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's worth mentioning that there's a Mage book (it might be Storyteller's Handbook Rev.) that discusses a period of time in Mage history roughly around the 1800's when it was <i>all the rage</i> to make Frankenstein-type monsters (which based on my limited understanding of CoD, is essentially what <i>Prometheans</i> are). In any case, as I recall the text referred to this time period as like a rueful thing--like people were making these creatures left and right and it was constant bother or annoyance.<br /> <br /> May be worth looking into!</div> </div> </div> </div>It gets better: the section in question was called \u201cthe Promethean Plague\u201d, and the Frankenstein monsters that it featured were referred to as Prometheans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T18:24:37-07:00","id":916528,"title":"","content":"While these have all been interesting ideas, they're not what I had in mind; I was thinking about an independent gameline, similar to P:tC, but not identical. Not a Mage spin-off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":6138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","user":"Mangle77","date":". 06-17-2016, 09:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-17T20:24:35-07:00","id":916593,"title":"","content":"I don't think a Promethean gameline for the original World of Darkness needs to be all that similar to PtC, beyond the protagonists being artificial beings that were given life by their creators. My own take on the notion would be to replace PtC's Pilgrimage with a struggle for freedom: every Promethean was created for a purpose, namely to serve their creator. Indeed, they weren't created as Prometheans <i>at all</i>; they were created as automatons, constructs, and flesh golems: things designed to serve their masters. And for most of them, that's the end of the story. <br /> <br /> But then there are those who have an encounter with Prometheus. Not literally the Titan of Greek mythology, but rather a force that chooses automatons and imbues them with a Spark that grants them a measure of free will. Sometimes Prometheus intervenes during the creation of a new automaton, and it awakens on the slab as a Promethean; other times, a Promethean finds an already existing automaton and imbues it with a bit of her own Spark. Either way, the result is a new Promethean that has her own desires and wishes, above and beyond service to her creator.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T08:45:30-07:00","id":918641,"title":"","content":"You can add to your game all you want, but if WoD has got too many supernatural creatures, then it becomes a &quot;Jurasic Park&quot; for gothic monsters. I wouldn't be WoD but something like Castlevania videogames, Buffy vampire slayer or Ravenloft rpg. WoC is about monster hidden among humans. More creatures means secret more difficut to be covered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Tell me what you brag and I will tell you what you lack&quot; (Spanish saying)<br /> <br /> \u00abThe Master Confucius said: \u201cThe noble man is in harmony but does not follow the crowd. The inferior man follows the crowd, but is not in harmony\u201d\u00bb (Anaclet 13:23)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11152-luis-carlos","name":"Luis Carlos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"258"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T10:39:19-07:00","id":918687,"title":"","content":"If you go with the notion I'm proposing, a <b> Promethean</b> game wouldn't add to the supernatural population at all, since there are already artificial beings out there. <b> Promethean</b> would merely select a subset of the non-sapient ones to be self-aware.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T14:57:27-07:00","id":918816,"title":"","content":"And using mages to introduce them it's not new, after all, same happened with Mummy. And they aren't an extension of Mage, if anything, mummies have more Vampire/Wraith elements in their outlook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-21T17:27:32-07:00","id":918876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/911496-a-promethean-gameline-for-owod?p=916593#post916593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think a Promethean gameline for the original World of Darkness needs to be all that similar to PtC, beyond the protagonists being artificial beings that were given life by their creators. My own take on the notion would be to replace PtC's Pilgrimage with a struggle for freedom: every Promethean was created for a purpose, namely to serve their creator. Indeed, they weren't created as Prometheans <i>at all</i>; they were created as automatons, constructs, and flesh golems: things designed to serve their masters. And for most of them, that's the end of the story.<br /> <br /> But then there are those who have an encounter with Prometheus. Not literally the Titan of Greek mythology, but rather a force that chooses automatons and imbues them with a Spark that grants them a measure of free will. Sometimes Prometheus intervenes during the creation of a new automaton, and it awakens on the slab as a Promethean; other times, a Promethean finds an already existing automaton and imbues it with a bit of her own Spark. Either way, the result is a new Promethean that has her own desires and wishes, above and beyond service to her creator.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bYeah, that's about the level of similarity I was thinking of. Maybe some of the alchemy stuff. I really like your &quot;automatons granted sentience&quot; idea. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-22T02:30:20-07:00","id":919007,"title":"","content":"Going with Dataweaver's vision - you could have distinctions based on how they dealt with their creators.<br /> -Killed their creator<br /> -Tricked their creator into freeing them / Fled their creator<br /> -Abandoned by creator<br /> -Absent creator<br /> -Hard to classify - like 'Killed their creator by accident' or 'Creator died before they own eyes, but not by their hand.'<br /> -Freed by creator<br /> <br /> &quot;This creature - an automaton with no agency yesterday - is obviously sentient now...And so, possess the ability to make choices...but <i>what kind of choices would it - he, she? - make if it had the chance to do so?</i> There is only one way to find out - I shall set it free into the world!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 06-22-2016, 06:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T19:57:47-07:00","id":955373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/951524-building-a-new-monster?p=951576#post951576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we are going to start more or less from scratch:<br /> <br /> <b>X-Splats:</b> Type of created you are: <b>Artificial</b> (like golems or galateas, you are an animated statue), <b>Mechanical</b> (robots that gained sentience and a semblance of actual life) <b>Biological</b> (clones and homunculus, you were &quot;grown&quot; in a lab) <b>Reanimated</b> (either one corpse or various sewn toghether)</div> </div> </div> </div>I rather like this idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T17:23:22-07:00","id":956009,"title":"","content":"oh curious How you think Garou would feel about them, think they'd bear wyrm taint?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T18:28:04-07:00","id":956049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/911496-a-promethean-gameline-for-owod?p=956009#post956009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh curious How you think Garou would feel about them, think they'd bear wyrm taint?</div> </div> </div> </div>They wouldn't be thrilled. Though I think only the possibly reanimated ones would be inherently Wyrm tainted. <br /> <br /> I quite like the the groupings <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar195_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"195\" data-vbnamecard=\"195\">Thorbes</a> suggests.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T22:00:13-07:00","id":956151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/911496-a-promethean-gameline-for-owod?p=919007#post919007\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going with Dataweaver's vision - you could have distinctions based on how they dealt with their creators.<br /> -Killed their creator<br /> -Tricked their creator into freeing them / Fled their creator<br /> -Abandoned by creator<br /> -Absent creator<br /> -Hard to classify - like 'Killed their creator by accident' or 'Creator died before they own eyes, but not by their hand.'<br /> -Freed by creator<br /> <br /> &amp;quot;This creature - an automaton with no agency yesterday - is obviously sentient now...And so, possess the ability to make choices...but <i>what kind of choices would it - he, she? - make if it had the chance to do so?</i> There is only one way to find out - I shall set it free into the world!&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>All of these assume that the creator is no longer around. My thought was that he's still here, and that how you gain your independence is, by default, a story yet to be told. In the meantime, he's an active part of the chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T09:03:23-07:00","id":956350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/911496-a-promethean-gameline-for-owod?p=956151#post956151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of these assume that the creator is no longer around. My thought was that he's still here, and that how you gain your independence is, by default, a story yet to be told. In the meantime, he's an active part of the chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does make it a bit harder to try to put together a PC-sized group (a &quot;mess&quot; of Prometheans?). Unless they all have the same creator, which seems a bit off-kilter or a very very specific story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T10:04:01-07:00","id":956392,"title":"","content":"It's not that different from the way every Lost changeling has a Keeper and a fetch.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T19:20:06-07:00","id":956697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/911496-a-promethean-gameline-for-owod?p=956009#post956009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh curious How you think Garou would feel about them, think they'd bear wyrm taint?</div> </div> </div> </div>Again possibly the reanimated corpse might be an issue and the robot will probably ping of the weaver. However I see a few traditions having a bit of a problem with them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T21:58:45-07:00","id":956780,"title":"","content":"I don't see why there would be Wyrm-taint for <i>any</i> of these; the reanimated corpse involves treating body parts in a manner analogous to machine parts, reassembling a broken machine, and jumpstarting the engine to get it running again. The result is machine-like because the process doesn't account for the soul, and thus the animated being lacks a will of its own. It ends up going through the motions and obeying the commands of its master. In that regard, they're no different from mechanical entities. Golems (I don't like the term \u201cArtificial\u201d because they're <i>all</i> artificial) involve using magic to imbue an inanimate object with mobility and enough cognitive ability to make at least rudimentary decisions \u2014 but again, there's nothing akin to a soul here, no free will; just a magical equivalent to a robot. The Biological ones are the most iffy in this regard; but we don't know at what point a human being gets a soul, so it's entirely possible that the processes that create a homunculus or a clone bypass that step. And for the purposes of <b>World of Darkness: Promethean</b>, I'd assume that the homunculi and clones featured in the game <i>didn't</i> get souls and, like all the rest, are machine-like. <br /> <br /> They'd all have Weaver-taint in a Werewolf crossover, because they're all fundamentally static things going through programmed routines \u2014 until Prometheus intervenes and grants them the Spark, which would oppose but not immediately purge the Weaver-taint.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T19:32:05-07:00","id":958004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/911496-a-promethean-gameline-for-owod?p=956392#post956392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not that different from the way every Lost changeling has a Keeper and a fetch.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Keeper who they have escaped. That's key to the backstory in Lost. It would be a very different game if each character was still with his/her/its Keeper Beyond the Hedge. And that's the analogy between a Lost game and the &quot;you are all still with your separate Victors&quot; Promethean game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T15:15:54-07:00","id":958445,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ajax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/911496-a-promethean-gameline-for-owod?p=958004#post958004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A Keeper who they have escaped. That's key to the backstory in Lost. It would be a very different game if each character was still with his/her/its Keeper Beyond the Hedge.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/My_Life_with_Master\" target=\"_blank\">An indie game, in fact.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}